Because Orlando Health requires that all of their Pet Therapy Teams be registered with a recognized national organization, the first step  to becoming an Orlando Health Pet Therapy Team is to decide which organization is right for you-  there are three choices. 

Pet Partners: www.petpartners.org
Therapy Dogs Inc.: www.therapydogs.com
Therapy Dogs International: www.tdi-dog.com

Spend some time on each web site learning about each organization's respective process. I'm an evaluator for Pet Partners so if you choose this organization I can help facilitate your process. We hold Pet Partner evaluations approximately every three months. Please contact me to learn more about Pet Partners and for information on the next evaluation. 

Once you are registered, please visit the Orlando Health web site and fill out the online Volunteer Application for the hospital of your choice. Please indicate that you have interest in Pet Therapy in your application. We will then contact you and schedule a time for you and your dog to come in for an interview.  If that all goes well, then you would shadow an existing Pet Therapy team, and then an existing handler would mentor you during your first session with your dog. 

After a successful shadowing and mentoring process you and your dog would be ready to begin volunteering on your own.  Also important to note that only the adult hospitals are currently accepting new pet therapy teams. 

A few important requirements to note - 
The Program requires that all Pet Therapy Volunteers visit the hospital at least two times per month. 
Your dog must be bathed and groomed within 24 hours prior to each visit. 
You must be at least 18 years old.

For Volunteer Application links, please visit the pages below according to facility:

